From 8a04546f1d38d9130f6e3cf36c353276ca3ffc05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: outfoxxed <outfoxxed@outfoxxed.me>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:54:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm: keep the picture an output shows at startup
 (AQ_SPLASH_ADOPT)

A boot splash that hands the display over to the compositor leaves its
last frame on screen. Taking the output over replaced that frame at once
with our first, unrendered one.

With AQ_SPLASH_ADOPT=1:
- a connector found while the backend starts, whose CRTC is active with
  its primary plane scanning out on it, adopts that picture and the mode
  it is shown in;
- commits in that mode leave the primary plane alone until one brings a
  rendered frame, so the configuration needs no modeset if nothing else
  changes. A commit in another mode, a disable, a CRTC change or a session
  deactivation ends the adoption, and the output commits as before;
- such a commit is not the one a test of the same state checks, which
  carries the primary plane. If the kernel refuses it, the adoption ends
  and the commit goes again as a modeset with the plane, as without one;
- IOutput::showsAdoptedPicture() says which outputs still show such a
  picture, e.g. for the compositor to hold its frames back until its own
  cover is up.

Setting the variable vouches that whatever is lit at startup may stay on
screen: a console that a lastclose restored would be adopted too.
---
